# Virtual environments
.venv/

# Python bytecode and caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# macOS
.DS_Store

# IDE and editor settings
.vscode/
.cursor/

# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.control

# Downloaded market data (regenerated by the downloader)
data/raw/*.csv

# Local reference copies of official backtest artifacts (snapshots,
# stop-walk-forward, mfe_mae holding-path output, etc.) used to run
# real-data tests locally. Not source, not official output -- never
# committed.
data/backtests/

# Research-candidate artifacts (universe snapshots, automated quality/
# correlation/backtest-sanity reports) explicitly tagged
# RESEARCH_CANDIDATE_NOT_OFFICIAL inside each file. Same status as
# data/backtests/ above -- local only, never committed.
#
# EXCEPTION: the cross-sectional-momentum-native-proxy PRE-REGISTRATION
# artifact is deliberately committed for real -- unlike the
# RESEARCH_CANDIDATE_NOT_OFFICIAL snapshots above, it is a frozen,
# performance-blind record (status=FROZEN_BEFORE_MARKET_DATA_FETCH_AND_BACKTEST)
# written and committed BEFORE any market data fetch or backtest result
# exists, and its entire evidentiary value depends on that commit being
# real and durable, not local-only. The corresponding RESULT artifact
# (equity_cross_sectional_momentum_native_proxy_result_*.json) is NOT
# exempted here -- it stays gitignored/local like every other
# data/research/ artifact unless a future task explicitly commits it.
#
# `data/research/*`, not `data/research/`, deliberately -- git cannot
# re-include a file via `!pattern` below if a PARENT DIRECTORY itself is
# excluded (confirmed via `git check-ignore -v`, not assumed); excluding
# only the directory's contents, not the directory entry itself, is what
# makes the negation exception below actually take effect.
data/research/*
!data/research/equity_cross_sectional_momentum_native_proxy_preregistration_*.json

# Live-trading runtime state (position state, decision logs, reports)
# plus the emergency STOP/FREEZE flag files scripts/run_daily_decision.py
# and scripts/run_crypto_stop_monitor.py check for -- was already
# untracked in practice but never actually excluded here (confirmed by
# checking, not assumed). Made explicit so a git-based deploy (pull/
# checkout/clean) can never delete or overwrite a live flag file or the
# real runtime state it protects.
data/live/

# V2-pivot research files -- untracked, not yet committed. Ignored here
# so a clean-working-tree check (e.g. scripts/deploy_control_arm_release.sh's
# own dirty-tree guard) isn't blocked by them. TEMPORARY, pending Levent's
# decision on whether these are committed later -- see the session report
# that added this block for the open question.
#
# src/research/pit_universe/ deliberately NOT listed here (was, briefly,
# and that was wrong): it is a real runtime dependency of
# src/live/issuer_identity_preflight.py and
# scripts/generate_control_universe_identity_anchors.py, not unrelated
# research -- ignoring it would silently break `git archive`-based
# deploys with ModuleNotFoundError on the control arm's first real run.
# Committed for real instead.
#
# src/research/batch_fetch_pilot/, src/strategy/strategy_config.py, and
# src/research/cross_sectional_momentum/ ALSO deliberately removed from
# this list (Levent's explicit approval, 2026-08-21, same "no longer a
# draft, real content" precedent as pit_universe/ above): batch_fetch_pilot/
# now holds a real, already-run feasibility pilot plus
# identity_safe_batch_fetch.py (closes its own documented FB/META
# ticker-recycling gap); strategy_config.py now holds TREND_RSI's real
# SignalRules/RiskManagementRules, drift-tested against the frozen
# engine; cross_sectional_momentum/ is the equity cross-sectional 12-1
# momentum native-universe proxy study (provenance confirmed with
# Levent 2026-08-21). All three committed for real instead.
docs/SHARED_CACHE_LAYER_DESIGN_V1.md
docs/UNIVERSE_MECHANISMS_MAP.md
docs/UNIVERSE_ROBUSTNESS_STEPS.md
src/research/backtest_metadata.py
src/research/grid_trading_prototype/
src/research/performance_report_v1/
